  clock: 5  # b636
  nonce: b636  # b636
  message: "DONE, PR #1183 (merged 2026-09-24, f77cb8af47).\n\nCORRECTION TO THIS ROW'S DIAGNOSIS: the callback symbols were positioned correctly, WITH the offset. The LOOKUP lacked it. Its key named a line `line_offset` lines above the callback, and in koel's HotkeyListener.vue another callback started at that line and column, so it was credited: _cb_onKeyStroke at 40-40 credited with calls at 44-46. Where nothing started there, the walk went on to the enclosing function or the file.\n\nFIX: the callback branch of js_ts._get_enclosing_function adds line_offset, like every other branch.\n\nDECISION (the row asked which attribution is wanted): .vue/.svelte now match .js. A callback is credited with its own calls, which is the WI-zavad design the _cb_* symbols exist for.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE:\n- test_js_call_anchor.py::test_a_vue_callback_is_credited_with_its_own_calls. It was red on dev (the call at line 6 was credited to the file) and is green with the fix. Collision, fall-through and in-span cases are all asserted.\n- A/B: analyze_javascript from a pinned dev worktree vs the fix, calls edges keyed by (path, dst, line):\n    koel            OUT->in 9 (all in HotkeyListener.vue), file->callback 279\n    chatwoot        enclosing fn->callback 7\n    podman-desktop  file->callback 78, enclosing fn->callback 11\n    workadventure   file->callback 55, enclosing fn->callback 15\n    gitlab          file->callback 2, enclosing fn->callback 115\n  On every repo, 0 edges were added or lost and 0 moved in->out.\nInstruments: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/pizan_09242026/ (ab.py, diff.py, DIFF.txt)."  # b636
